# Cooldown channels (server/README.md "Cooldown channels"). Owner, 2026-10-16: attack spells, healing spells, the auto
# attack and moving things must have cooldowns that never conflict: using one never delays or blocks another. Stock
# 1.4 kept one next-action time and one queued task per player for every item use, item move and step, and the auto
# attack's queued check (classicAttackSpeed = false) shared that task: an attack rune held a healing rune and every
# potion for 1 s (timeBetweenExActions), a potion held the next rune, a step or a use held the distance attack, an item
# move or a use cancelled the queued attack check (the next swing waited for the 1 s creature think) and the attack
# check cancelled a queued use or move (dropped). Now a player has a cooldown channel per kind of action (enums.h
# CooldownChannel_t), each with its own next-action time and queued task:
#   ACTION   plain uses (doors, levers, tools, food, containers) and walking: the stock nextAction and delays
#   MOVE     item and creature moves, the equip hotkey, the right-click equip (0024): moveItemDelay (50 ms) after each,
#            and a step holds it as before
#   ATTACK / HEAL / SUPPORT   rune uses by the rune spell's group (attack + special / healing / support):
#            runeChannelDelay (1000 ms) after a rune of the same group only
#   POTION   items named with Game.setItemCooldownChannel(id, COOLDOWN_CHANNEL_POTION) (data/scripts/chaos/
#            cooldown_channels.lua: the base potion script's items and the Everfull potions): potionChannelDelay (1000 ms)
# The auto attack has its own queued check (Player::setNextAttackTask) and only a step that is not a kite walk step
# (0028) holds a distance swing; the swing interval (getAttackSpeed, 0011 floor and cap) is unchanged. Spells never used
# the next-action time; their spell and group cooldowns stay as spells.xml sets them. Every channel keeps a floor of
# 50 ms and one queued task, so packet floods and fast clients stay limited per channel. New config: cooldownChannels
# (default true; false is the stock shared delay), moveItemDelay, runeChannelDelay, potionChannelDelay (configKeys too).
# Guard: tools/cooldown_channels_patch_test.py (CI). Applies after 0001-0041.
